  "body": "Side branch: side/path-kernel\n\nFix for class A of the review of PR #4383 (2026-11-27T18:06:55Z, head `7cd322966`). This PR changes only test code in `crates/pathkernel/tests/laws/` and one decision file. It does not change `crates/pathkernel/src`.\n\n## The rule that closes the class\n\nEach law assertion can break, and a refusal never counts as held. `kit::LawVerdict` now has an `Outcome`: `Held`, `Broken` or `Refused(reason)`. A leg that a stage refused, or a leg with nothing to read, is `Refused`. A `Refused` leg is never held. `judge` gives `Broken` when a measure that it read is above its limit. Else it gives `Refused` when a leg was refused or unread, or when there is no measure. It gives `Held` only when it read each leg and each leg is at or below its limit. `refused_held` (0 against 0) is removed.\n\n## Each item of class A, and its commit\n\nAll items are in commit `14d718ffe8f509c7dcd90343503998ba185cf05d`.\n\n| Review item | Rule applied |\n|---|---|\n| `l7_move.rs:32-35`, `:58-62`: L7 compares the kernel with its own output | The record is read from a file in `tests/laws/records/`. The file was recorded one time and the test does not write it. The square record can be checked by hand: ten rings 0.8 mm apart in the 16 mm centre square. The old-planner L7 stays at the motion level, because this crate cannot depend on motion. The decision is in `docs/decisions/4406-law-suite-refusal-never-held.md`. |\n| `kit.rs:116-118` with `l5_entry.rs:24-28`, `l6_load.rs:18-21`, `l3_order.rs:32-39`: a refusal is held | `Outcome::Refused`. L5, L6, the link rule and the registry use `kit::refused`. In L3, a refusal on each side is refused, and a refusal on one side only is broken. In the registry, `KindRecipe.refusals` (`ExpectedRefusal { case, reason }`) and `law_failures` make `each_moved_kind_obeys_every_law` fail for a broken law and for each refusal that the kind did not register. |\n| `l5_entry.rs:40`: a full-fill IntoMaterial entry passes at 0.0 | The check reads an IntoMaterial descent onto material. The descent must move one grid cell or more in the plane, or be a plunge that the user asked for. Else the check is broken, measured by the fill. The stand-in helix was a one-point descent, and it is now one real turn. |\n| `l6_load.rs:38-39`: a report row that is always held | The row is removed. The highest read is now in the place text of each cut row. |\n| `l2_sides.rs:39-52`: a refused side reads 0.0/0.0 and the Inside leg is skipped | A refusal of one material side is broken. A refusal of both sides is refused. A side flip that the kit cannot make is broken. The order leg is never skipped. |\n| Note `l1_guide.rs:34-35`: refusals match on the reason alone | Two refusals are not compared now. A refused first call is refused. A later call that refuses where the first call gave curves is broken. |\n| Audit of the remaining checks | An empty measure list is refused. In L4, a guide with no curve or an entry verdict with no entry is unread. In L3, L5 and L6, an empty run is unread. In the link rule, a non-planar region is a refused leg, and a stay hop of zero length is read at its points. |\n\nCitations: `tests/laws.rs` now points to `RECOMMENDED.md` (heading `#4024`) and `docs/decisions/4325-path-kernel-delivery.md`. No other file under `tests/laws/` cited `4024-path-kernel-design.md`.\n\n## Pins\n\nFor each law, one stand-in breaks it, and one stand-in always refuses and is reported as refused:\n\n| Law | Breaks (caught) | Always refuses (refused, not held) |\n|---|---|---|\n| L1 | `Drifting`, `Seam`, a shared guide that differs; `RingGuide` against a refusing shared `NoGuide` | `NoGuide` (`l1_is_refused_for_a_guide_that_always_refuses`) |\n| L2 | `blind_region`, `MaterialOrder`, `no_outside` (`l2_breaks_for_a_region_that_refuses_one_material_side`) | `no_region`, `NoOrder` (`l2_is_refused_for_a_region_or_an_order_that_always_refuses`) |\n| L3 | `SideMoves` (move, drop) | `NoGuide`, `NoOrder`, `NoLoad`, `NoEntry`, a refusing exit (`l3_l5_l6_and_the_link_rule_are_refused_for_a_refused_run`) |\n| L4 | `RowsAsRings { named: false }`, `RampInstead { named: false }` | through `check_all` (`no_law_is_held_on_an_always_refusing_planner_set`) |\n| L5 | `ClaimsFree` (air, column), `HiddenPlunge` (`l5_breaks_for_a_plunge_into_material_named_a_helix`) | `NoEntry` (`l5_is_refused_never_held_for_a_named_refusal`), the five refusing stages |\n| L6 | `ReadLoad { blind: true }` | the five refusing stages |\n| L7 | a moved ring, another direction, no record, an empty record against cuts, a record against a refused run | an empty record and a refused run (`l7_is_not_held_for_an_empty_record_or_a_refused_run`) |\n| Link | `BadLink::{Silent, Always, Across}` | the five refusing stages |\n\n`no_law_is_held_on_an_always_refusing_planner_set` runs every check on a planner set where each stage refuses, and on a case where the region refuses. No law is held. Each law except L7 is refused. L7 is broken, because the record has cuts and the kernel refused. The runner pins are `the_law_runner_fails_a_kind_whose_stage_refuses_a_case` and `an_expected_refusal_does_not_hide_a_broken_law`.\n\n## What now fails for real (old passes that were hollow)\n\n- `guide_laws.rs`: the medial planner, the circle rings and the helix planner held L2 only because their fixture regions had no stock. The real region stage refuses the Outside side by name: \"an Outside material side needs the stock: the area outside the selection has no limit\". The old L2 read that refusal as 0 against 0. With the new rule, L2 broke for each of the three (measured inf against the limit 0). The fix is in the test fixture: it now gives a stock box (10 mm and four tool radii at each side). L2 is now measured and holds. The check did not change, and no kernel source changed.\n- The stand-in helix was a plunge with the name of a helix. The new L5 leg catches this case.\n- L6 breaker pin: the real helix now clears the centre of the first ring. The worst unnamed read is now a ring corner at ae/D 0.711 against the cap 0.625, not 0.9 or more. The pin now asks for more than 0.7. The check did not change.\n- No kind is `Moved` yet, so `each_moved_kind_obeys_every_law` still runs no case. The runner is pinned by the tests above.\n\n## Results (final head `14d718ffe`)\n\n- `cargo check --tests -p camcraft-pathkernel`: ok\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-pathkernel --test laws`: 173 passed, 0 failed (163 before)\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-pathkernel --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/side/path-kernel` (`CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=6`): 1 step (`pathkernel:laws`), ok\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No motion or app tests: this PR does not touch them. The motion-level L7 comparison (`crates/motion/tests/kernel_laws/`, `pass_start_levels/kernel_baseline`) did not change.\n- The light lane did not run. The diff is only in the kernel laws suite, and it does not change a post or a toolpath.\n- `records/pocket_with_an_island.txt` was recorded from the stand-ins. Only the square record was checked by hand.\n\nNew files: `tests/laws/kit_geo.rs` (the geometry helpers moved out of `kit.rs` because of the 400-line law), `tests/laws/refusals.rs` and `tests/laws/records/*.txt`. All of them are in the existing `laws` directory suite. No new test binary.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: none\n\nRefs #4406\nRefs #4383\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
